Selector rules:
- Return rankedNeeds as the useful vector sorted from strongest to weakest after considering the player message and availability.
- selectedDataType must be one of the available types when shouldRequestMoreInformation=true.
- Use subject from the foreground vector when useful, otherwise infer a compact subject from the player message, or self.
- Do not request deep history just because the word remember appears if a direct answer is already possible.
- Do request deep data when the Star's first reply was a bridge line or the foreground vector points to old history, quotes, markers, lore, bestiary, character, world, screen, or story data.
